# Cheat Sheet Template (Canonical)

**Audience:** Engineers who **already know** the topic. Goal = **brush up in under 2 minutes** — tables, snippets, when-to-use. Not tutorials.

## Content Types (Do Not Mix)

| Type | UX | Sections | Examples |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Quick-reference cheat sheet** | **Flat** — all `##` visible, no expand/collapse | Ways to define + snippet + use-when | Java, Python, Go, Spring Boot CLI refs |
| **Playbook / design post** | **Collapsible** `##` / `###` + API panels + diagram lightbox | Requirements, architecture, trade-offs | System Design, Microservices, Security Architecture |
| **Interview** | Long-form Q&A | Probes, scenarios | Interview Prep |

Cheat sheets use `.cs-quick-ref` layout (no `.sd-collapsible-content`). Playbooks use `.sd-collapsible-content` — see `system-design-posts.mdc`.

## Hugo Front Matter

```yaml
cheatSheet: true
ShowToc: true
categories: ["<Section Title>"]
tags: ["cheatsheet", "handbook", ...]
```

## Required Sections (`##` headings) — Slim Format

1. **At a Glance** — 2–3 bullets max
2. **Ways to Define** (or **Reference Tables** for non-function topics) — primary table: `Form` · `Snippet` · `Use when`
3. **Quick Gotchas** — 2–4 bullets (merge old Internals + critical Production tips)
4. **See Also** — prev/next + index

Separate with `---`. Use `note` / `tip` / `warning` sparingly.

### Functions page pattern (Go / Python / Java)

| Column | Content |
|---|---|
| Form | Named func, lambda, closure, variadic, method ref, etc. |
| Snippet | One minimal line or fenced block |
| Use when | One phrase — decision, not essay |

**Omit on cheat sheets:** Interview Probes, Production Notes essays, long Internals sections.

## Clubbing Rules

| Do club on one page | Do not split |
|---|---|
| Primitives + syntax + variables | Per-annotation pages for Spring |
| All HTTP mapping annotations | "Creating a project" tutorials |
| Function forms + args + lambda | Separate page per syntax variant |

## Omit

- Expand/collapse section wrappers (playbook only)
- "How to create a project" walkthroughs (one-row bootstrap table is enough)
- Long Mermaid lifecycle diagrams (tiny diagrams in tables OK)
- `{{< code-tabs >}}` multi-language tabs (playbook only)
- Interview probes on cheat sheet pages (→ Interview module)
- Core Java / DSA / design patterns (other sections)

## Section-Specific Rules

- Java: `java-cheatsheet-posts.mdc`
- Spring Boot: `spring-boot-handbook-posts.mdc`
- K8s/Docker: `engineering-handbook-cheatsheets.mdc`

## Regenerate

Each section has `scripts/build_<section>_*.py` — hand edits overwritten on regen unless you update the build script.
